{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T08:33:31.744Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"eda2446424a05ba568a1cb08","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T08:33:31.744Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review follow-up on PR #1635 (CodeRabbit full review of f86d1539e, 2026-10-31): the `tests_omitted.restore_with` command had three scope gaps.\n\n1. **Shell safety.** `--pm-path` was emitted bare or inside JSON double quotes, so a path such as `/tmp/$HOME` (or one containing backticks) would expand when copied into a shell. The command is now rendered by the shared `renderPmCommand` / `quoteCommandArg` helpers, which escape `$`, backticks, quotes and backslashes on POSIX and use CommandLineToArgvW quoting on Windows.\n2. **Extension scope.** A narrowed run under `--no-extensions` produced a restore command that re-enabled extensions. The receipt now carries `--no-extensions` when the invocation used it.\n3. **Tracker scope.** A tracker selected through `PM_PATH` has no `--path` flag, so the restore command omitted it and could read a different tracker in the next shell. `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope` keeps the resolved root as `--pm-path` when `PM_PATH` selected it; a tracker found by discovery stays implicit.\n\n`renderTrackerPathFlag` is replaced by `renderLinkedTestRestoreCommand(itemId, scope)` plus `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope(global, pmRoot)` in `src/sdk/test/execution-receipts.ts` (keeping `src/sdk/test/execution.ts` under the 3400-line cap). Evidence: `tests/unit/sdk/test/execution-receipts.spec.ts` (posix `$`/backtick escaping, win32 quoting, `--no-extensions`, PM_PATH vs discovery) and `tests/unit/commands/test/test-command.spec.ts`, which replays the emitted command and gets all three linked tests back.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T08:33:31.744Z"}],"before_hash":"5906a07e50e3e40ef7c5fc6264238ab5544f2a7d8f997aff5bea0264a4b8ee04","after_hash":"ff2a4dfb56d672dcb7153b3123cb7d998cfc8f2a10907113e01940580a9c0803","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e4e28fdaf8815be5bac3382e7bb832c941536bd0cb7b26a027eb698a8ac2103a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T09:50:29.103Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"eda2446424a05ba568a1cb08","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_edit","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/2/text","value":"Review follow-up on PR #1635 (CodeRabbit full review of f86d1539e, 2026-10-31): the `tests_omitted.restore_with` command had three scope gaps.\n\n1. **Shell safety.** `--pm-path` was emitted bare or inside JSON double quotes, so a path such as `/tmp/$HOME` (or one containing backticks) would expand when copied into a shell. The command is now rendered by the shared `renderPmCommand` / `quoteCommandArg` helpers, which escape `$`, backticks, quotes and backslashes on POSIX and use CommandLineToArgvW quoting on Windows.\n2. **Extension scope.** A narrowed run under `--no-extensions` produced a restore command that re-enabled extensions. The receipt now carries `--no-extensions` when the invocation used it.\n3. **Tracker scope.** A tracker selected through `PM_PATH` has no `--path` flag, so the restore command omitted it and could read a different tracker in the next shell. `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope` keeps the resolved root as `--pm-path` when `PM_PATH` selected it; a tracker found by discovery stays implicit.\n\n`renderTrackerPathFlag` is replaced by `renderLinkedTestRestoreCommand(itemId, scope)` plus `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope(global, pmRoot)` in `src/sdk/test/execution-receipts.ts` (keeping `src/sdk/test/execution.ts` under the 3400-line cap). Evidence: `tests/unit/sdk/test/execution-receipts.spec.ts` (posix `$`/backtick escaping, win32 quoting, `--no-extensions`, PM_PATH vs discovery) and `tests/unit/commands/test/test-command.spec.ts`, which replays the emitted command and gets all three linked tests back.\n\nSecond review round: `docs/TESTING.md` now tells readers to copy and run the complete `tests_omitted.restore_with` command rather than a bare `pm test <item-id> --list`, which would drop `--pm-path` and `--no-extensions`. PowerShell expansion of `$(...)` and backticks inside win32 double quotes affects every rendered recovery command, not only this one, so it is tracked separately in pm-kjoudp instead of patched per call site."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2/edited_at","value":"2026-10-31T09:50:29.103Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T09:50:29.103Z"}],"before_hash":"ff2a4dfb56d672dcb7153b3123cb7d998cfc8f2a10907113e01940580a9c0803","after_hash":"d683b100481ab07d8be377c1e283e71144d435207524b891e91b99f2dffd7061","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5c735fff652434ec61f2bea1a5a5cd95571dca04e99309b65a458eacacd55be4"}
